{"id":"views-look","window":["2016-10-24","2022-12-30"],"intro":["No view's next-session drift stands out from its own shifted-view placebo. The best, carry and the equal-weight combo, earn about +0.016 sigma a session (annual Sharpe about 0.25). Simply being long all ten instruments earned +0.016 too.","Power is the real limit. Over 6.2 years and 10 instruments, the smallest drift we could detect is 0.03-0.04 sigma a session (Sharpe 0.45-0.6). That is the size of the published premia, so this window can neither confirm nor rule them out.","Drift builds with horizon, as the monthly papers would predict: the combo reaches +0.08 per sqrt-session at 20 sessions and mom12 reaches +0.05. Every horizon still sits under the combo placebo's 95th percentile (0.15 at 20 sessions).","Vol state barely moves the hit rate. The combo hits 52.9% in low sigma, 51.2% in mid and 51.7% in high, all within about +/-1.6pp of 50%. Carry did not crash in high vol in 2016-22 (skew +0.04, against -0.17 in low vol); rates were near zero and differentials small.","The level races match the theory. A Sharpe-0.25 view should move P(its line first) by 0.2-0.8pp. The measured shifts run from -1.0 to +1.1pp, with intervals of about +/-1pp, and all sit inside the placebo.","The views are mostly independent: sign correlations across families run from -0.15 to +0.21. That makes an equal-weight combo the natural form, but it did not beat carry alone here.","For now a view is a tilt (which side, how big), not a trigger. At 1 sigma lines a Sharpe-0.25 view is worth about 0.016 sigma per race, against roughly 0.04 sigma for one spread."],"charts":[{"type":"bars","title":"Next-session return in the view's direction, by view","unit":"daily sigma","ref":0,"note":"Mean of sign(view) x open-to-close return, all 10 instruments pooled, 95% date-block bootstrap interval. Benchmark: the grey-label rows, the same view shifted by a random 1-4 years (200 draws, 5th-95th pct), and always-long. A Sharpe-0.5 view would sit at +0.03 sigma.","rows":[{"label":"mom1 (n 16,016)","value":-0.0004,"lo":-0.0261,"hi":0.0238},{"label":"mom1 placebo 90% band","value":0.0061,"lo":-0.0153,"hi":0.0298},{"label":"mom3 (n 16,018)","value":0.0111,"lo":-0.011,"hi":0.0342},{"label":"mom3 placebo 90% band","value":0.0062,"lo":-0.0232,"hi":0.0338},{"label":"mom12 (n 14,998)","value":0.0029,"lo":-0.0247,"hi":0.0305},{"label":"mom12 placebo 90% band","value":0.0107,"lo":-0.0251,"hi":0.0424},{"label":"carry (n 11,121)","value":0.0159,"lo":-0.0042,"hi":0.0368},{"label":"carry placebo 90% band","value":0.0105,"lo":-0.0068,"hi":0.0255},{"label":"surprise (n 16,022)","value":0.0091,"lo":-0.0168,"hi":0.0334},{"label":"surprise placebo 90% band","value":0.0007,"lo":-0.0194,"hi":0.0217},{"label":"combo (n 12,547)","value":0.0161,"lo":-0.0081,"hi":0.0427},{"label":"combo placebo 90% band","value":0.0146,"lo":-0.0143,"hi":0.0428},{"label":"always long (base drift)","value":0.0156,"lo":-0.0032,"hi":0.0335}]},{"type":"lines","title":"Horizon sweep: view-signed return per sqrt(day)","unit":"sigma x sqrt(h)","xlabel":"horizon (sessions, open to open)","note":"Return over h sessions in the view's direction, divided by sigma x sqrt(h), so a constant drift per day would rise as sqrt(h). Benchmark: the combo's shifted-view placebo 95th percentile at each horizon (100 draws; it sits above 0 because views and drift persist). Overlapping windows: points at h>1 are not independent.","series":[{"name":"mom12","points":[[1,0.0045],[2,0.0068],[5,0.0152],[10,0.0351],[20,0.0507]]},{"name":"carry","points":[[1,0.0041],[2,0.0056],[5,0.0072],[10,0.0146],[20,0.0346]]},{"name":"combo","points":[[1,0.0177],[2,0.0221],[5,0.0365],[10,0.0704],[20,0.0806]]},{"name":"combo placebo 95th pct","points":[[1,0.0318],[2,0.0397],[5,0.0644],[10,0.0839],[20,0.1543]]}]},{"type":"lines","title":"Year by year: next-week return in the view's direction","unit":"sigma x sqrt(5)","xlabel":"year","note":"Each point pools the 10 instruments for one year (2016 = 24 Oct to 30 Dec only). Benchmark: 0. A stable view keeps one sign across years; look for sign flips. One year holds about 50 independent weeks.","series":[{"name":"mom3","points":[[2016,0.0196],[2017,0.0416],[2018,0.0575],[2019,-0.0467],[2020,0.0546],[2021,-0.0483],[2022,0.0444]]},{"name":"mom12","points":[[2017,0.0501],[2018,-0.1073],[2019,0.0109],[2020,0.1029],[2021,-0.0389],[2022,0.0817]]},{"name":"carry","points":[[2016,0.0699],[2017,-0.1157],[2018,0.0031],[2019,-0.005],[2020,0.052],[2021,0.0884],[2022,0.011]]},{"name":"combo","points":[[2016,0.0906],[2017,-0.0109],[2018,0.0741],[2019,-0.0287],[2020,0.1445],[2021,0.0116],[2022,0.0223]]}]},{"type":"groups","title":"Per instrument: next-week return in the view's direction","names":["mom12","carry","surprise"],"unit":"sigma x sqrt(5)","note":"Benchmark: 0, and the per-instrument noise: one instrument over 6 years has about 300 independent weeks, so the 95% band is about +/-0.11. Carry is 0 (not defined) for gold and the indices.","rows":[{"label":"EURUSD","values":[0.0276,-0.0012,0.0801]},{"label":"GBPUSD","values":[0.0132,0.0098,0.06]},{"label":"AUDUSD","values":[0.0441,0.0996,0.0319]},{"label":"NZDUSD","values":[0.0199,-0.0242,0.0124]},{"label":"USDJPY","values":[0.0016,0.066,0.0529]},{"label":"USDCAD","values":[-0.0616,-0.0557,0.0517]},{"label":"USDCHF","values":[-0.0349,-0.0415,0.0377]},{"label":"GOLD","values":[-0.0131,0,0.1019]},{"label":"NQ","values":[0.0963,0,-0.0048]},{"label":"SPX500","values":[0.0588,0,0.0496]}]},{"type":"bars","title":"Combo view: rank IC with next-week return, per instrument","unit":"Spearman IC","ref":0,"note":"Bar = the instrument's IC. The whisker here is NOT a confidence interval: it is the 5th-95th percentile of the same IC with the view shifted by a random 1-3 years (200 draws). A bar outside its whisker beats the placebo at 10% two-sided, one test of ten.","rows":[{"label":"EURUSD","value":0.0546,"lo":-0.1387,"hi":0.123},{"label":"GBPUSD","value":0.0454,"lo":-0.1171,"hi":0.1